# Cloud Infrastructure & Automated Log Aggregation Capstone Project

## Project Overview

This project implements a secure, automated log aggregation pipeline using Amazon Web Services (AWS).

The solution transfers log files from a private EC2 instance to a public EC2 instance through VPC peering and SSH, then automatically uploads the received logs to an Amazon S3 bucket.

The process is automated using Linux cron jobs, allowing log transfers and S3 uploads to run every minute without manual intervention.

The project demonstrates practical knowledge of cloud networking, infrastructure deployment, access management, secure file transfers, object storage, encryption and automation.

## Project Objectives

- Create separate private and public AWS VPC environments.
- Deploy EC2 instances in their respective subnets.
- Establish connectivity between the VPCs using VPC peering.
- Configure routing between private and public networks.
- Transfer logs securely using SSH and SCP.
- Configure an EC2 IAM instance role for AWS service access.
- Store log files in a private Amazon S3 bucket.
- Enable server-side encryption for stored logs.
- Automate log transfers and S3 uploads using cron.

