### Data Flow

1. The private EC2 instance generates or maintains the source log file.
2. A scheduled cron job transfers the log to the public EC2 instance using SCP.
3. The public EC2 instance uses its attached IAM role to authenticate with AWS.
4. Another scheduled cron job uploads the received log to Amazon S3.
5. The S3 object is stored with AES256 server-side encryption.

