## IAM Configuration

An EC2 IAM role named `devops-s3-role` was created and attached to the public EC2 instance through the `devops-s3-instance-profile` instance profile.

The role allows the EC2 instance to authenticate with AWS services without storing long-lived access keys on the server.

The identity was verified using:

```bash
aws sts get-caller-identity
```

Verified identity:

```text
Account: 818788518694
Arn: arn:aws:sts::818788518694:assumed-role/devops-s3-role/i-01c2490ba6155a53f
```

**Security note:** The role was attached successfully using the AmazonS3FullAccess managed policy because the lab IAM user could not create the requested inline policy. A production implementation should replace this broad permission with a bucket-scoped least-privilege policy.

## Log Transfer Implementation

### Source Log

The private EC2 instance contains:

```text
/var/log/boots.log
```

Log contents:

```text
Hello from devops KKE!
```

### SSH and SCP Transfer

A dedicated SSH key named `log-transfer` was generated on the private EC2 instance.

The corresponding public key was authorized on the public EC2 instance.

The private EC2 instance transfers the log using:

```bash
scp -i /home/ubuntu/.ssh/log-transfer \
  -o BatchMode=yes \
  -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes \
  /var/log/boots.log \
  ubuntu@10.20.1.98:/home/ubuntu/boots.log
```

The transfer was verified on the public EC2 instance.

## Automation with Cron

Two cron jobs automate the pipeline.

### 1. Private EC2 — Log Transfer

```cron
* * * * * /usr/bin/scp -i /home/ubuntu/.ssh/log-transfer -o BatchMode=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes /var/log/boots.log ubuntu@10.20.1.98:/home/ubuntu/boots.log >> /home/ubuntu/log-transfer.log 2>&1
```

This transfers the source log to the public EC2 every minute.

### 2. Public EC2 — S3 Upload

```cron
* * * * * /usr/bin/aws s3 cp /home/ubuntu/boots.log s3://devops-s3-logs-770304373/devops-priv-vpc/boot/boots.log >> /home/ubuntu/s3-upload.log 2>&1
```

This uploads the received log to S3 every minute.

The cron service was verified as active on the private EC2.

